    title: "[Refractory-Cancer and Immunotherapy-Combination Lane + Randomized-Trial Multi-Modal Readout of Neoadjuvant Durvalumab With or Without Stereotactic Body Radiotherapy in Early-Stage NSCLC + Pathological Response Correlated With a Reduction in Chromosomal Instability and Hence Reduced Tumour Heterogeneity in Responders + 11 Recurring Transcriptional Meta-Programs Nominated as the Resistance Structure With Hypoxia, EMT, DNA-Damage Repair and Unfolded-Protein Response Attached to Mono- and Combination-Therapy Failure + Spatial Transcriptomics Showing Those Resistance Meta-Programs Occupying Near-Mutually-Exclusive, Niche-Localized Territories + Responders to Dual Treatment Showing a Higher Fraction of Dominant B/Plasma-Cell Clones, Reduced T and NK Cells Across the Differentiation Spectrum, and Enrichment of M2-Like Macrophages and Pathological Cancer-Associated Fibroblasts] GSE302960 'Multi-modal single-cell, spatial, and genomic analyses of NSCLC patients treated with neoadjuvant durvalumab with or without stereotactic body radiotherapy [Spatial]' (Homo sapiens, score 9 = joint-top of today's scan, n=15 deposited libraries from 43 patients, pdat 2026/11/21 = FRESHEST NOVEL accession band of the day, raw CSV + JPG + JSON + MTX + PNG + TIFF + TSV, license NCBI public repository) + [Anti-Fibrotic and Multi-Omics Lane + Rheumatic Mitral Valve Disease Reframed as Autoimmune Inflammation Sustaining Chronic Fibrotic Remodelling Rather Than As Passive Valve Damage + Tissue-Centric Multi-Omics Combining Histopathology, Unbiased Proteomics of Human Mitral Valve Tissue (n=72) and External Plasma Proteomics (n=445) + 1,436 Differentially Expressed Proteins Enriched in ECM Remodelling, Immune Response, Haemostasis and Multi-Growth-Factor Signalling Including TGF-Beta and IGFBP Pathways + Cross-Species Validation in a Murine Autoimmune Valvular Carditis Model With scRNA-seq + Mechanistic Closure in Primary Human Valvular Interstitial Cells and 3D Mitral-Valve Mimetics Showing TGF-Beta Inducing IGFBP5, IGFBP7 and CCN2 and Their Silencing Attenuating Collagen Expression] GSE355175 'Integrative Multimodal Analysis of Rheumatic Mitral Valve Disease Identifies Insulin-Like Growth Factor Binding Proteins as Profibrotic Drivers' (Homo sapiens, score 6, n=10 deposited libraries, pdat 2026/11/21, raw CSV, license clean) + [Peptide-Adjacent Small-Molecule and Platinum-Resistance Lane + A Beta-Carboline Scaffold Extended With a Triazole Ring to Yield Seven Analogues (CBN-123-26, -30, -39, -45, -59, -63, -64) as Small-Molecule Agents Against Platinum-Resistant High-Grade Serous Ovarian Carcinoma + CCK-8 and EdU Screening Narrowing to CBN-123-39 and CBN-123-59 as the Two Potent Candidates + Proliferation, Migration and Invasion Suppressed in Both Hits by CCK-8, Colony Formation, Transwell and Wound-Healing Assays + Transcriptome Sequencing Plus DEG, Enrichment and PPI-Network Analysis Attributing the Activity to Inhibition of Cell-Cycle and DNA-Replication Pathways] GSE355101 'Inhibitory effects of beta-carboline-triazole derivatives on the proliferation and invasion of high-grade serous ovarian carcinoma' (Homo sapiens, score 6, n=9 deposited libraries, pdat 2026/11/21, raw TXT, license clean) are three NOVEL signals whose shared thesis is THAT THE UNIT OF DISCOVERY TODAY IS A NAMED MECHANISM WITH A READOUT ALREADY ATTACHED - a randomized-trial multi-modal program that identifies the resistance structure of a real combination regimen, a tissue-centric proteomic-hierarchy record that names profibrotic mediators inside human valve tissue, and a chemically explicit small-molecule series with a transcriptionally attributed mechanism in platinum-resistant disease - rather than another descriptive atlas or a ranked gene list.",
